From fe411be30d50e60422309f974668dfa9b71206f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AshFall UI <ui@ashfall.local>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:24:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Settings: PlayTime indicator page on Battery
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

AshFall #137: the Settings side of the native PlayTime indicator. One row on
Settings > Battery with a live estimate (2h 45m · 5.4W, or Off) opening a
PlayTimeSettings sub-screen with the placement, detail, time format, sample
window/interval, charging symbol/cycle, tap-cycle, font size and battery
capacity rows, plus a non-selectable live read-out.

Values are stored in persist.ashfall.batt.* as the wave-2 contract fixes them
(docs/phase6.md §9.3), SystemUI owns the defaults, and an unset or malformed
property falls back to the documented default instead of failing the page.

The live values come from the framework BatteryManager (the sticky
ACTION_BATTERY_CHANGED broadcast plus CURRENT_NOW / CHARGE_COUNTER and the
power profile), not from ashfall.status.*: there is no battery sampler in
ashfall-hwd, because a coredomain cannot read sysfs_batteryinfo (platform
neverallow) and the RP5 power-supply nodes are vendor-labeled.

The row is declared in res/xml/power_usage_summary.xml because that is the
battery page that renders in this tree: the metadata screens
(PowerUsageSummaryScreen / PowerUsageSummaryApiScreen) are gated behind the
catalyst_power_usage_summary_screen and catalyst_migration_26q3 aconfig flags,
which are disabled.

Copy pass (#155): text only. The Show indicator summary no longer explains where
the estimate comes from, Tap to cycle and Charging cycle are one plain sentence
each, "meters" is "values" in the row and in the toast, and the estimate rows
read "Average over" / "Update every" instead of the engine's window/sampling
wording. Values, layout, preference keys and placeholders are unchanged.
